    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths has always been a passion for me—it’s like solving puzzles where every equation feels like unlocking a new part of logic. I enjoy the precision and creativity it demands, especially in physics, which aligns with my love for structured thinking. It’s both challenging and rewarding, much like running or birdwatching requires patience but brings deep satisfaction.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really—I find maths grounding rather than overwhelming. My high conscientiousness score suggests I’m methodical, which helps me break problems into manageable steps. Anxiety usually comes from complexity, not the subject itself. I trust my ability to tackle it logically.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "No, but I’ve seen tools like Wolfram Alpha or symbolic solvers help others visualize steps. For me, math feels intuitive—AI might be unnecessary unless explaining concepts to someone unfamiliar. My low openness score means I prefer hands-on learning over digital shortcuts.",
